  "TourPoints": [
    {
      "Id": "cffb54db-aef9-4b7f-84f5-fb1be3b5fa6a",
      "Description": "Many cameras in TiXL are defined by a position and a target."
    },
    {
      "Id": "d259159c-15a8-4646-82ba-a95b4e1db3da",
      "Description": "TiXL activates these and the other parameters so they will be used for all connected operators."
    },
    {
      "Id": "ac9c84bb-7f3e-4aef-aa12-75a13294583e",
      "Description": "Once again, TiXL coordinate system is defines...\n- *X* as left right\n- *Y* as Up\n- *Z* as forward"
    },
    {
      "Id": "ab31b5a9-3ee1-4c51-a1e1-d444f975acf6",
      "ChildId": "8f5b538f-60e2-4c47-a2e3-9d13ae1270aa",
      "InputId": "313596cc-3854-436b-89da-5fd40164ce76",
      "Description": "Notice how the **Z position** of the camera is 2.414. \n\nThat's by design, because it will perfectly frame a 1 unit object positioned in world center."
    },
    {
      "Id": "b0bee9c9-767a-42d3-bc65-0176b2e3c7ca",
      "Description": "Because Camera are always \"activated\" seeing them as gizmo in the scene requires a special setup that we will cover later."
    },
    {
      "Id": "a742983d-9fab-44ec-a76e-9a41c8825444",
      "ChildId": "8f5b538f-60e2-4c47-a2e3-9d13ae1270aa",
      "InputId": "313596cc-3854-436b-89da-5fd40164ce76",
      "Description": "Please position the [Camera] to match the solution.",
      "Style": "CallToAction"
    }
  ]
}